Subject: [PATCH 09927/11362] Record why 52 deterministic-replay tests are RED,
 and escalate the choice

An investigation into two failing `result == replay` tests found the scope was
much larger and the cause was not what the brief assumed.

Measured: 68 test files assert `result == replay`; 52 of those tests fail.
Two structural causes, neither a provenance break:

A. The fabrication gate stamps `flagged_adversarial` / `corrigendum_pending`
   into an artifact after the module wrote it. The module never emits those
   keys, so whole-artifact equality can never hold again. exp5342 landed clean
   at 2d4d50af13 (37 keys) and was stamped at 1e9bee1412 ten minutes later
   (39 keys).

B. The artifact records a sha256 over whole shared, high-churn files. Spec-first
   discipline requires every later experiment to append to the same capability
   spec, so the hash is guaranteed to go stale. exp5342's spec hash broke at
   268b2376d5 -- exp5355, the next experiment in the same capability, same day.

Of the 63 replay-tested modules with a present artifact: 3 carry a gate stamp
the module never writes, 50 hash at least one shared high-churn file, 2 have
both. exp5342 has both.

No fix is applied. Every available fix is an operator call: resolving receipts
against the artifact's own commit makes the receipt agree by construction and
does nothing for cause A; ignoring the checksum or stamp fields deletes the
guard; regenerating the artifacts is an evidence write under results/**.

Also recorded: a narrower REQ-section-scoped receipt was measured, is stable for
the 14 self-learning cases, and has a hole -- it cannot see an upstream
requirement being edited or deleted. Written down so it is not re-derived.

Own the process error: the first scan here grepped one helper name,
`source_artifact_checksums`, and concluded the pattern was extinct. It is not.
24 modules use the renamed `source_file_checksums`, and experiment_6597 shipped
this morning hashing CLAUDE.md, research-references.md and exclusion_manifest
.yaml. A pattern list narrower than its concept -- the bug class this project
already has a discipline about. An independent adversarial review caught it.

Mutation marker 39e7fd55 retired deliberately, not by reverting. Its own
attribution was `attributed_to_run: []` with `unattributed:
["ops/conductor-log.md"]`, no `results/` path anywhere in it, and that file had
gained exactly one conductor log row (2026-08-25 17:15 UTC, "Plan milestone
2026.08.576") written by the live conductor pid 4062753. Reverting it would have
destroyed a running agent's work, which is the failure the guard's own CAUTION
describes.

